This looks like December 2017 or possibly January 2018. Fed funds at 1.42% matches December 2017 (the rate was 1.30–1.42%). The unemployment rate of 4.1% matches both November and December 2017. CPI of 2.23% YoY matches November 2017 (2.2%), while core CPI at 1.71% matches November or December. The 10-year yield at 2.43% fits late November or December 2017. The VIX at 10.18 is low, and the dollar is down 6% YoY.

Payrolls over 3 months averaging 170k fits November 2017. The 12m equity return of 21.3% is consistent with November 2017 (S&P up about 22%). The 1m equity return of 2.1% fits November 2017 (+3.1%) or December (+1.1%), so it is unclear which. The 2-year yield at 1.91% fits end of December 2017 (1.88%), and end of November was 1.78%. Fed funds effective at 1.42% is more consistent with December (after the December hike, effective was 1.42%). The 10-year yield ended December at 2.40%. I'll go with December 2017.

